The `Plant` enum doesn't have a `fromChar` method. I'll add a private helper method in `KindergartenGarden` to map characters to `Plant` enum values.

KindergartenGarden.java
```
import java.util.List;
import java.util.Arrays;
import java.util.ArrayList;

class KindergartenGarden {

    private final String[] rows;

    private static final String[] STUDENTS = {
        "Alice", "Bob", "Charlie", "David", "Eve", "Fred",
        "Ginny", "Harriet", "Ileana", "Joseph", "Kincaid", "Larry"
    };

    KindergartenGarden(String garden) {
        this.rows = garden.split("\n");
    }

    List<Plant> getPlantsOfStudent(String student) {
        int index = Arrays.asList(STUDENTS).indexOf(student);
        if (index == -1) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Unknown student: " + student);
        }
        int col = index * 2;
        List<Plant> plants = new ArrayList<>();
        plants.add(plantFromChar(rows[0].charAt(col)));
        plants.add(plantFromChar(rows[0].charAt(col + 1)));
        plants.add(plantFromChar(rows[1].charAt(col)));
        plants.add(plantFromChar(rows[1].charAt(col + 1)));
        return plants;
    }

    private Plant plantFromChar(char c) {
        switch (c) {
            case 'G': return Plant.GRASS;
            case 'C': return Plant.CLOVER;
            case 'R': return Plant.RADISH;
            case 'V': return Plant.VIOLET;
            default: throw new IllegalArgumentException("Unknown plant character: " + c);
        }
    }
}
```
